{"duration_api_ms":206276,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8d2e0e65-7702-4317-9772-49c736a5664b","total_cost_usd":0.253686,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16088,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":18933,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":14060},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16088,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":18933,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16088,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16088},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":18933,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":16088,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.253686,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":14060,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The feasible front is essentially one line: D=3.384-3.385, B=1.2, cone=70 (all at their caps), with flight path angle gamma swept from -1.5 to -3.57. Peak g reaches 12 at gamma near -3.57. Heatshield mass fraction caps D near 3.3853, and the cd_fore surrogate hull caps B near 1.2. Normalised hypervolume has stalled at about 0.3555 over rounds 4-6 (gains of 1e-3, 3e-4, 2e-4). Because the flux reference is 2.5e6 and front fluxes are 227k-275k, hypervolume is driven almost entirely by bondline temperature. Fine spacing along gamma and the corner point matter more than any other region.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-d091f610d31f (D 3.385, gamma -3.5695): flux 274560, T 391.09, g margin 1.3e-4, mass-fraction margin 1.4e-4. This is the corner design, pinned by g and mass fraction.\",\"C-c3f9f333f061 and C-9690b44cafcb: mass-fraction margin goes 8.6e-5 to 2.7e-5 as D goes 3.3851 to 3.3852, so the D cap is about 3.38525.\",\"C-3da7d9bac3e7 and C-eed229743768: g rises about 1.6-1.7 per deg near -3.5, and T falls about 10 K/deg.\",\"C-363a563b3536 (D 3.3): flux 285110, T 392.49 against 274.5k and 391.1 at D 3.385. Smaller D is worse in both objectives.\",\"C-94a9f7a46f9b and C-1618bda1fac0: g is close to independent of B and cone, and rises only about 0.4 per metre of D. Stepping to smaller D therefore buys almost no extra gamma.\",\"C-0202524b57fd, C-5b57439845df, C-3d41ce848a30 and C-05beb8f06d5f: B above 1.2 at cone 70 falls outside the surrogate hull. C-3cd51d4bc9fc: cone 66 with B 1.2 is invalid geometry. Both are cap-like limits.\",\"C-7a7d7f365bcc (D 3.38, B 1.19): mass-fraction margin 0.0028 against about 0.0031 expected at B 1.2, so lower B slightly raises mass. It also gives a slightly higher flux and T.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak g depends almost entirely on gamma (about 1.65 per deg near -3.57, less at shallow angles). That sets a fixed steepness cap, which in turn sets the minimum T reachable. Larger D lowers ballistic coefficient and raises nose radius, so flux and T both fall, but the mass-fraction limit stops D at about 3.385. Higher B and cone have the same helpful effect and sit at the hull and variable bounds. Mass fraction scales roughly as D squared and worsens slightly as cone or B drop. The optimum is therefore a fixed corner. Remaining improvement is limited to filling gamma gaps on the line, nudging gamma to the g cap, and a few probes of cone and B near the corner. This is based on the data; the Rn^-0.5 stagnation scaling is prior knowledge and was not needed for these picks.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Line-interpolated predictions are reliable to a few hundred W/m2 and a few tenths of a K. The corner points (gamma -3.5700) sit within about 1e-4 of the g and mass-fraction limits, so a feasibility flip is possible. The cone and B probes could trigger a geometry or hull failure, since the boundary between cone 66 (invalid) and cone 69.5 (valid) is unknown. The cone and B sensitivities are only weakly identified from confounded rows. I do not expect any hidden basin, but I cannot rule one out in unexplored corners.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-189e84c63d67\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the shallow end of the front between gamma -1.5237 and -1.65 on the D 3.384, B 1.2, cone 70 line.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":229300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":416.25,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Cheap, well-interpolated front-fill point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f3bf2be39d48\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.70 and -1.80.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.75},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":232340,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413.84,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves front coverage in the flux direction.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a5b057e49731\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the 0.25 deg gap between gamma -1.85 and -2.10.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.95},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":236600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410.78,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front-fill point in a wide gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a5b057e49731\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap at gamma -2.05, between -1.85 and -2.10.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.05},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":238800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":409.28,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front-fill point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-bd7900cd2a82\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.10 and -2.30.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":242190,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":407.13,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front-fill point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-d105815e0ee3\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.30 and -2.40.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.35},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":245600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405.05,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front-fill point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-afca1e3dbf91\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.45 and -2.65.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":250300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402.44,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front-fill point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-da46e0051200\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap at gamma -2.70, between -2.65 and -2.75.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":253830,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400.56,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front-fill point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-117f5236e520\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.85 and -2.95.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.9},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":258590,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.18,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front-fill point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b6ad04910306\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.95 and -3.10.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":261000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.04,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front-fill point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-2148af2e8391\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap at gamma -3.20, between -3.10 and -3.25.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":265800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.85,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front-fill point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e9fb95df2518\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -3.30 and -3.42.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.35},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":269400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front-fill point near the g limit, with g about 11.63 so feasible.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-64fb038bccfd\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -3.42 and -3.48.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":271800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.28,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front-fill point with g about 11.80, so feasible.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3da7d9bac3e7\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -3.48 and -3.52.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.79,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Dense sampling near the corner, where hypervolume is most sensitive.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-16ffc81dbe96\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -3.52 and -3.56 at D 3.384, where the mass margin is 7e-4.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"A point just before the g cap, with g about 11.97.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-d091f610d31f\",\"rationale\":\"Push gamma 0.0005 deg past the current corner at D 3.385. Extrapolated g is about 11.9993, just under the limit of 12, so it should still be feasible and give a tiny T gain.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.57},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274570,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.08,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests how tight the corner is. Feasibility margin is about 1e-4, so it is worth a higher-fidelity check.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-9690b44cafcb\",\"rationale\":\"Corner variant at D 3.3852 (mass margin 2.7e-5) with gamma -3.5700, to test the mass and g tolerances together.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.57},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274530,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the mass-fraction limit and g limit simultaneously. It is unlikely to add hypervolume but bounds the corner.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-16ffc81dbe96\",\"rationale\":\"Probe the cone sensitivity: cone 69.0 with slightly smaller D (3.37) to keep mass-fraction margin positive. Tests whether cone has any T benefit other than through D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.37,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":277500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Cone effect on flux and T is confounded in current data. This checks for a non-monotonic cone benefit and probes the geometry boundary.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7a7d7f365bcc\",\"rationale\":\"Probe the B sensitivity: lower B to 1.15 at D 3.38 with gamma -3.55. Lower B raises mass slightly, but D 3.38 leaves about 0.003 of margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":276700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Quantifies B sensitivity away from the hull edge. This checks that B 1.2 is the best value.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":166822,"type":"result","duration_ms":206316,"uuid":"0485c50b-db25-4644-9f42-019e5af3a132","ttft_stream_ms":1515,"time_to_request_ms":35,"first_content_frame_ms":1515,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
